      "headline": "Treaty of Tordesillas",
      "text": "On June 7, 1494, the Treaty of Tordesillas was signed, dividing the newly discovered lands outside Europe between the Portuguese Empire and the Spanish Empire along a meridian 370 leagues west of the Cape Verde islands.",
      "date": "1494-06-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Vasco Núñez de Balboa's Pacific Discovery",
      "text": "In 1513, Vasco Núñez de Balboa crossed the Isthmus of Panama and became the first European to see the Pacific Ocean from the New World, proving that the Americas were separate from Asia.",
      "date": "1513"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hernán Cortés Conquers the Aztec Empire",
      "text": "In 1521, Hernán Cortés completed the conquest of the Aztec Empire, marking a significant expansion of Spanish influence in the New World.",
      "date": "1521"
    },
