      "text": "The smiley face murder theory was introduced by retired New York City detectives Kevin Gannon and Anthony Duarte, along with Dr. Lee Gilbertson, in the late 1990s. They proposed that the deaths of 45 young men found in bodies of water across several Midwestern American states were not accidental drownings but rather the work of one or more serial killers.",
      "date": "1990s"
    },
