      "headline": "First Public Mention",
      "text": "The theory gained public attention in 2008 when Gannon and Duarte presented their findings, suggesting a connection between the deaths and graffiti of smiley faces found near the locations where the bodies were discovered.",
      "date": "2008"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Media Coverage and Criticism",
      "text": "The theory received significant media coverage, but also faced criticism from law enforcement and other experts who argued that the evidence was circumstantial and not sufficient to support the claims of a serial killer or killers.",
      "date": "2008"
    },
    {
