    {
      "headline": "Chicano Movement",
      "text": "The Chicano Movement, also known as El Movimiento, gained momentum in the 1960s. It was a civil rights movement extending the Mexican American civil rights movement of the 1940s with the stated goal of achieving Mexican American empowerment.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Chicano Moratorium",
      "text": "On August 29, 1970, the Chicano Moratorium, a movement of Chicano activists that organized anti-Vietnam War demonstrations, held a major protest in East Los Angeles. It was one of the largest anti-war protests by any ethnic group in the United States.",
