      "headline": "Publication of 'Michelle Remembers'",
      "text": "In 1980, the book 'Michelle Remembers' was published. Co-written by Canadian psychiatrist Lawrence Pazder and his patient Michelle Smith, it used the controversial practice of recovered-memory therapy to make claims about satanic ritual abuse involving Smith.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Beginning of the Satanic Panic",
      "text": "The publication of 'Michelle Remembers' in 1980 marked the beginning of the Satanic Panic, a moral panic involving allegations of widespread Satanic ritual abuse.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "McMartin Preschool Trial",
      "text": "In 1983, the McMartin preschool trial began in California, one of the most publicized cases of alleged Satanic ritual abuse. It involved accusations against the staff of the McMartin preschool, leading to a lengthy and costly trial.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peak of the Satanic Panic",
      "text": "By the late 1980s, the Satanic Panic had reached its peak, with numerous allegations and cases of supposed Satanic ritual abuse being reported across the United States.",
      "date": "1980s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the McMartin Preschool Trial",
      "text": "In 1990, the McMartin preschool trial ended with no convictions. The case had lasted seven years and cost $15 million, becoming the longest and most expensive criminal trial in American history at the time.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "FBI Report on Satanic Ritual Abuse",
      "text": "In 1992, the FBI released a report concluding that there was no evidence to support the existence of widespread Satanic ritual abuse in the United States.",
      "date": "1992"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of the Satanic Panic",
      "text": "By the late 1990s, the Satanic Panic began to decline as skepticism grew and many of the allegations were discredited.",
      "date": "1990s"
    }
  ]
}

