      "headline": "Coining of the Term 'Beatnik'",
      "text": "In 1958, San Francisco Chronicle columnist Herb Caen coined the term 'beatnik' as a derogatory label for the followers of the Beat Generation. The name was inspired by the Russian suffix '-nik', which was used to denote members of various political or social groups.",
      "date": "1958"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peak of the Beatnik Subculture",
      "text": "The beatnik subculture was at its most prevalent in the 1950s. Beatniks were known for their anti-materialistic lifestyle, rejection of conformity and consumerism, and expression through various forms of art, such as literature, poetry, music, and painting.",
      "date": "1950"
    }
  ]
}

