    {
      "headline": "Earliest Recorded Practices",
      "text": "The earliest recorded practices of qigong date back to the Shang dynasty (1600–1046 BCE) where it was used as a form of health exercise.",
      "date": "-1600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development During the Zhou Dynasty",
      "text": "During the Zhou dynasty (1046–256 BCE), qigong practices were further developed and integrated into traditional Chinese medicine and philosophy.",
      "date": "-1046"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Integration with Daoism",
      "text": "In the Warring States period (475–221 BCE), qigong was integrated with Daoist philosophy, emphasizing the cultivation of qi for spiritual enlightenment.",
