      "headline": "Battle of Jutland Begins",
      "text": "The Battle of Jutland commenced on the afternoon of 31 May 1916. It was a naval battle between Britain's Royal Navy Grand Fleet, under Admiral Sir John Jellicoe, and the Imperial German Navy's High Seas Fleet, under Vice-Admiral Reinhard Scheer.",
      "date": "1916-05-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Engagement",
      "text": "The first engagement of the battle occurred in the late afternoon of 31 May 1916, involving the British battlecruiser squadron under Vice-Admiral Sir David Beatty and the German battlecruisers under Vice-Admiral Franz von Hipper.",
      "date": "1916-05-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Main Fleet Engagement",
      "text": "The main fleets of both the British and German navies engaged in battle during the evening of 31 May 1916. This was the largest naval battle of World War I.",
      "date": "1916-05-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Night Action",
      "text": "During the night of 31 May to 1 June 1916, both fleets engaged in sporadic fighting. The darkness and confusion led to several encounters between smaller ships.",
      "date": "1916-05-31"
