      "headline": "Birth of Solomon Northup",
      "text": "Solomon Northup was born in July 1808 in Minerva, Essex County, New York. He was the son of Mintus Northup, a freed slave, and a free woman of color.",
      "date": "1808-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Anne Hampton",
      "text": "In 1829, Solomon Northup married Anne Hampton. The couple eventually had three children together.",
      "date": "1829"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kidnapping and Enslavement",
      "text": "In 1841, Solomon Northup was offered a job as a traveling musician and went to Washington, D.C. There, he was drugged and kidnapped into slavery. He was shipped to New Orleans and sold into slavery.",
      "date": "1841"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Enslavement in Louisiana",
      "text": "Solomon Northup was held as a slave for 12 years in the Red River region of Louisiana, mostly in Avoyelles Parish.",
      "date": "1841-1853"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Meeting Samuel Bass",
      "text": "During his enslavement, Solomon Northup met Samuel Bass, a Canadian carpenter working on the plantation. Bass helped Northup get word to his family in New York.",
      "date": "1852"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Regaining Freedom",
      "text": "Solomon Northup regained his freedom on January 3, 1853, after his family and friends, with the aid of the Governor of New York, Washington Hunt, secured his release.",
      "date": "1853-01-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Twelve Years a Slave'",
      "text": "In 1853, Solomon Northup published his memoir, 'Twelve Years a Slave,' which became a bestseller and contributed to the abolitionist movement.",
      "date": "1853"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Public Speaking and Abolitionist Activities",
      "text": "Following the publication of his memoir, Solomon Northup became active in the abolitionist movement, giving lectures and speeches about his experiences.",
      "date": "1853-1863"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Disappearance",
      "text": "The details of Solomon Northup's later life, including the date and circumstances of his death, remain unknown. He was last known to be alive in 1863.",
      "date": "1863"
    }
  ]
}

