    },
    {
      "headline": "First Laparoscopic Cholecystectomy",
      "text": "In 1985, Dr. Erich Mühe performed the first laparoscopic cholecystectomy, a gallbladder removal surgery, which became a standard procedure and popularized laparoscopic surgery.",
      "date": "1985"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Widespread Adoption of Laparoscopic Surgery",
      "text": "By the 1990s, laparoscopic surgery had become widely adopted for various procedures, including appendectomies, hernia repairs, and bariatric surgeries, due to its minimally invasive nature and quicker recovery times.",
      "date": "1990"
