      "headline": "Anglo-Zanzibar War",
      "text": "On August 27, 1896, the Anglo-Zanzibar War took place between the United Kingdom and the Sultanate of Zanzibar. It lasted between 38 and 45 minutes, making it the shortest recorded war in history.",
      "date": "1896-08-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zanzibar becomes a British Protectorate",
      "text": "In 1890, Zanzibar became a British protectorate following the Heligoland-Zanzibar Treaty, which was an agreement between the United Kingdom and Germany.",
      "date": "1890"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Sultanate of Zanzibar",
      "text": "The Sultanate of Zanzibar ended in 1964 when the Sultan was overthrown during the Zanzibar Revolution, leading to the establishment of the People's Republic of Zanzibar and Pemba.",
      "date": "1964"
    }
  ]
}

