      "text": "Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf?, a play by Edward Albee, was first staged in October 1962. The play explores the complexities of the marriage of a middle-aged couple, Martha and George, as they engage with a younger couple, Nick and Honey, after a university faculty party.",
