      "text": "Cedella Booker published her autobiography, 'Bob Marley: An Intimate Portrait by His Mother,' in 1997, providing personal insights into the life of her son.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Cedella Booker",
      "text": "Cedella Booker passed away on April 8, 2008, in Miami, Florida, at the age of 81.",
      "date": "2008-04-08"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the NBA Play-In Tournament",
      "text": "The NBA Play-In Tournament was introduced for the 2019-2020 season as a way to determine the final playoff seeds in the Eastern and Western Conferences. This was part of the league's response to the COVID-19 pandemic, which disrupted the regular season schedule.",
      "date": "2020"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First NBA Play-In Tournament",
      "text": "The first NBA Play-In Tournament took place in August 2020. It featured teams from the Western Conference, with the Portland Trail Blazers defeating the Memphis Grizzlies to secure the 8th seed in the playoffs.",
      "date": "2020-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion of the Play-In Tournament Format",
      "text": "For the 2020-2021 NBA season, the Play-In Tournament format was expanded to include both the Eastern and Western Conferences. Teams finishing the regular season in positions 7 through 10 in each conference competed for the 7th and 8th playoff seeds.",
      "date": "2021"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Full Season Play-In Tournament",
      "text": "The first full season of the expanded NBA Play-In Tournament took place in May 2021. It included teams from both conferences and determined the final playoff seeds for the 2021 NBA Playoffs.",
      "date": "2021-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Continuation of the Play-In Tournament",
      "text": "The NBA Play-In Tournament continued to be a part of the NBA postseason structure for the 2021-2022 season, solidifying its role in determining the final playoff seeds.",
      "date": "2022"
    }
  ]
}

