      "headline": "Birth of W. Somerset Maugham",
      "text": "William Somerset Maugham was born on January 25, 1874, in Paris, France.",
      "date": "1874-01-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Education in England",
      "text": "After spending his first ten years in Paris, Maugham was schooled in England.",
      "date": "1884"
    },
    {
      "headline": "University Studies in Germany",
      "text": "Maugham attended a German university, furthering his education.",
      "date": "1890"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Medical Student in London",
      "text": "Maugham became a medical student in London, pursuing a career in medicine.",
      "date": "1892"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Qualified as a Physician",
      "text": "In 1897, Maugham qualified as a physician, although he never practiced medicine.",
      "date": "1897"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of First Novel",
      "text": "Maugham's first novel, 'Liza of Lambeth', was published in 1897, attracting attention for its depiction of life in the slums.",
