      "headline": "Planning of Operation Downfall",
      "text": "Operation Downfall was the proposed Allied plan for the invasion of the Japanese home islands near the end of World War II. It was divided into two parts: Operation Olympic and Operation Coronet.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Olympic",
      "text": "Operation Olympic was intended to capture the southern third of the southernmost main Japanese island, Kyūshū. The operation was set to begin in November 1945, using the recently captured island of Okinawa as a staging area.",
      "date": "1945-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Coronet",
      "text": "Operation Coronet was the planned invasion of the Kantō Plain, near Tokyo, on the main Japanese island of Honshu. It was scheduled to occur in early 1946, with airbases on Kyūshū captured in Operation Olympic providing land-based air support.",
      "date": "1946"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cancellation of Operation Downfall",
      "text": "Operation Downfall was canceled following Japan's surrender after the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki, the Soviet declaration of war, and the invasion of Manchuria.",
      "date": "1945-08"
    }
  ]
}

