      "text": "According to the Hebrew Bible, Jaffa was conquered by the Israelites under King David around 1000 BCE.",
      "date": "-1000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Assyrian Conquest",
      "text": "In 701 BCE, Jaffa was conquered by the Assyrian Empire under King Sennacherib.",
      "date": "-0701"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Babylonian and Persian Periods",
      "text": "Jaffa was later controlled by the Babylonians and then the Persians after the fall of the Babylonian Empire in 539 BCE.",
      "date": "-0539"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hellenistic Period",
      "text": "Following the conquest by Alexander the Great in 332 BCE, Jaffa became part of the Hellenistic world.",
      "date": "-0332"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Rule",
      "text": "Jaffa came under Roman control in 63 BCE when Pompey the Great conquered the region.",
      "date": "-0063"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Byzantine Period",
      "text": "During the Byzantine period, Jaffa was an important Christian center.",
      "date": "0324"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arab Conquest",
      "text": "In 636, Jaffa was conquered by the Arab armies during the Muslim conquest of the Levant.",
      "date": "0636"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Crusader Rule",
      "text": "Jaffa was captured by the Crusaders in 1099 during the First Crusade and became part of the Kingdom of Jerusalem.",
      "date": "1099"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mamluk Period",
      "text": "In 1268, Jaffa was captured by the Mamluks, who destroyed its fortifications.",
      "date": "1268"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ottoman Rule",
      "text": "Jaffa became part of the Ottoman Empire in 1517 and remained under Ottoman control until the 20th century.",
      "date": "1517"
    },
