      "text": "Methotrexate was approved by the FDA for the treatment of cancer in 1953, following successful trials demonstrating its efficacy in treating various types of cancer.",
      "date": "1953"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction for Autoimmune Diseases",
      "text": "In the 1980s, methotrexate began to be used for the treatment of autoimmune diseases such as rheumatoid arthritis and psoriasis, expanding its therapeutic applications.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Approval for Rheumatoid Arthritis",
      "text": "Methotrexate was officially approved by the FDA for the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis in 1988, after clinical trials confirmed its effectiveness in managing the disease.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Approval for Psoriasis",
      "text": "In 1972, methotrexate was approved for the treatment of severe psoriasis, providing a new option for patients with this chronic skin condition.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Use in Ectopic Pregnancies",
      "text": "Methotrexate began to be used as a treatment for ectopic pregnancies in the 1980s, offering a non-surgical option for managing this potentially life-threatening condition.",
      "date": "1980"
    }
  ]
}

