      "headline": "Establishment of the Medieval Inquisition",
      "text": "The Medieval Inquisition was established in 1184 by Pope Lucius III with the papal bull 'Ad abolendam'. It was aimed at combating heresy, particularly targeting the Cathars and Waldensians.",
      "date": "1184"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Papal Inquisition",
      "text": "In 1231, Pope Gregory IX established the Papal Inquisition as a more centralized system to combat heresy, appointing inquisitors who were usually Dominican or Franciscan friars.",
