      "text": "The World Kickboxing Association (WKA) was established in 1976 to promote and regulate the sport of kickboxing worldwide.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of American Kickboxing",
      "text": "American kickboxing emerged in the 1970s, influenced by traditional karate and Western boxing. It became popular in the United States as a competitive sport and fitness activity.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the International Sport Kickboxing Association",
      "text": "The International Sport Kickboxing Association (ISKA) was formed in 1986 to oversee the sport of kickboxing globally, providing a framework for competitions and championships.",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kickboxing in the Olympics",
      "text": "Although kickboxing is not an official Olympic sport, it has been recognized by the International Olympic Committee and is included in the World Games, which feature sports not contested in the Olympics.",
      "date": "2000"
    }
  ]
}

