      "text": "In 1562, Teresa founded the Convent of Saint Joseph in Ávila, marking the beginning of her reform of the Carmelite Order.",
      "date": "1562"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Approval of the Discalced Carmelites",
      "text": "In 1567, Teresa received approval from the Carmelite General to establish more reformed convents, leading to the formation of the Discalced Carmelites.",
      "date": "1567"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of the First Discalced Carmelite Monastery for Men",
      "text": "In 1568, Teresa, along with John of the Cross, founded the first Discalced Carmelite monastery for men in Duruelo, Spain.",
      "date": "1568"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of 'The Interior Castle'",
      "text": "In 1577, Teresa completed her seminal work, 'The Interior Castle', which is considered one of the greatest works of mystical literature.",
      "date": "1577"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Teresa of Ávila",
      "text": "Teresa of Ávila died on October 4, 1582, in Alba de Tormes, Spain.",
      "date": "1582-10-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Canonization of Teresa of Ávila",
      "text": "Teresa was canonized as a saint by Pope Gregory XV on March 12, 1622.",
      "date": "1622-03-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Declared a Doctor of the Church",
      "text": "In 1970, Teresa of Ávila was declared a Doctor of the Church by Pope Paul VI, making her one of the first women to receive this honor.",
      "date": "1970"
    }
  ]
}

