      "text": "Antoine de Saint-Exupéry was born on June 29, 1900, in Lyon, France.",
      "date": "1900-06-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Flight Experience",
      "text": "In 1912, at the age of 12, Saint-Exupéry had his first flight experience, which sparked his lifelong passion for aviation.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Military Service",
      "text": "In 1921, Saint-Exupéry began his military service and trained as a pilot in the French Air Force.",
      "date": "1921"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published First Story",
      "text": "In 1926, Saint-Exupéry published his first story, 'L'Aviateur' (The Aviator), marking the beginning of his literary career.",
      "date": "1926"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published 'Southern Mail'",
      "text": "In 1929, Saint-Exupéry published his first novel, 'Courrier Sud' (Southern Mail), based on his experiences as an airmail pilot.",
      "date": "1929"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published 'Night Flight'",
      "text": "In 1931, Saint-Exupéry published 'Vol de nuit' (Night Flight), which won the Prix Femina literary prize.",
      "date": "1931"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Consuelo Suncin",
      "text": "On April 22, 1931, Saint-Exupéry married Consuelo Suncin, a Salvadoran writer and artist.",
      "date": "1931-04-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published 'Wind, Sand and Stars'",
      "text": "In 1939, Saint-Exupéry published 'Terre des hommes' (Wind, Sand and Stars), which won the Grand Prix du roman de l'Académie française.",
      "date": "1939"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published 'The Little Prince'",
      "text": "In 1943, Saint-Exupéry published 'Le Petit Prince' (The Little Prince), his most famous work, which became one of the best-selling books in history.",
      "date": "1943"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Disappearance and Death",
      "text": "On July 31, 1944, Saint-Exupéry disappeared during a reconnaissance mission over the Mediterranean Sea. His death was confirmed later, but the exact circumstances remain unknown.",
      "date": "1944-07-31"
    }
  ]
}

