      "text": "On July 3, 1866, the decisive Battle of Königgrätz (also known as the Battle of Sadowa) took place. The Prussian army, under the command of Helmuth von Moltke, defeated the Austrian forces, marking a turning point in the war.",
      "date": "1866-07-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Prague",
      "text": "The Treaty of Prague was signed on August 23, 1866, officially ending the Austro-Prussian War. The treaty resulted in the dissolution of the German Confederation and the exclusion of Austria from German affairs.",
      "date": "1866-08-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the North German Confederation",
      "text": "Following the war, the North German Confederation was established under Prussian leadership in 1867, laying the groundwork for the eventual unification of Germany.",
