    {
      "headline": "Color Restrictions",
      "text": "In the late 19th and early 20th centuries, several U.S. states enacted laws prohibiting the addition of yellow coloring to margarine to protect the dairy industry, forcing margarine producers to sell it in its natural white color.",
      "date": "1900"
