      "headline": "Naming of Gallium",
      "text": "Gallium was named by its discoverer, Paul-Émile Lecoq de Boisbaudran, after 'Gallia', the Latin name for France, in 1875.",
      "date": "1875"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Use in Electronics",
      "text": "Gallium began to be used in electronics in the 20th century, particularly in the form of gallium arsenide, which is a semiconductor material.",
      "date": "1900"
