      "text": "In the late 19th and early 20th centuries, the women's suffrage movement, driven by egalitarian ideals, fought for and achieved women's right to vote in many countries, including the United States in 1920.",
      "date": "1920"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Civil Rights Movement",
      "text": "During the 1950s and 1960s, the Civil Rights Movement in the United States sought to end racial segregation and discrimination, heavily influenced by egalitarian principles of equality and justice.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Human Rights",
