      "headline": "First Essex-class Carrier Commissioned",
      "text": "The first Essex-class aircraft carrier, USS Essex (CV-9), was commissioned on December 31, 1942.",
      "date": "1942-12-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Essex-class Carriers Enter World War II Combat",
      "text": "Essex-class carriers began seeing combat in mid-1943, playing a significant role in the Pacific Theater during World War II.",
      "date": "1943"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of World War II",
      "text": "By the end of World War II in 1945, 14 Essex-class carriers had seen combat. None were lost to enemy action, although several were damaged by kamikaze attacks.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-War Service and Modernization",
      "text": "After World War II, several Essex-class carriers were modernized to handle heavier and faster aircraft of the early jet age. This modernization extended their service life significantly.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service During the Korean War",
      "text": "Essex-class carriers were actively involved in the Korean War from 1950 to 1953, providing air support and engaging in combat operations.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Supercarriers",
      "text": "The introduction of supercarriers in the 1950s, 1960s, and 1970s gradually reduced the role of Essex-class carriers as the backbone of the U.S. Navy.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
