      "headline": "Milton S. Hershey founds the Hershey Chocolate Company",
      "text": "In 1894, Milton S. Hershey founded the Hershey Chocolate Company as a subsidiary of his Lancaster Caramel Company.",
      "date": "1894"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hershey Chocolate Company becomes independent",
      "text": "In 1900, Milton S. Hershey sold the Lancaster Caramel Company for $1 million, allowing him to focus solely on chocolate production.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hershey, Pennsylvania is established",
      "text": "In 1903, Milton S. Hershey began construction of a chocolate factory in Derry Church, Pennsylvania, which would later become known as Hershey, Pennsylvania.",
      "date": "1903"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hershey's Milk Chocolate Bar is introduced",
      "text": "In 1900, the Hershey's Milk Chocolate Bar was introduced, becoming the first mass-produced milk chocolate in the United States.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hersheypark opens",
      "text": "In 1906, Hersheypark was opened as a leisure park for the employees of the Hershey Chocolate Company.",
      "date": "1906"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hershey Trust Company is established",
      "text": "In 1905, Milton S. Hershey established the Hershey Trust Company to manage his wealth and support the Milton Hershey School.",
      "date": "1905"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Milton Hershey School is founded",
      "text": "In 1909, Milton S. Hershey and his wife, Catherine, founded the Milton Hershey School for orphaned boys.",
      "date": "1909"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hershey Chocolate Corporation is incorporated",
      "text": "In 1927, the Hershey Chocolate Company was reorganized and incorporated as the Hershey Chocolate Corporation.",
      "date": "1927"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hershey's Kisses are introduced",
      "text": "In 1907, Hershey's Kisses were introduced, becoming one of the company's most iconic products.",
      "date": "1907"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hershey's role in World War II",
      "text": "During World War II, Hershey produced a special chocolate bar, the D Ration, for U.S. troops, earning several Army-Navy 'E' Awards for excellence.",
      "date": "1941"
