      "headline": "Libya Temperature Record Decertified",
      "text": "In 2012, the World Meteorological Organization decertified a former record temperature that was measured in Libya, based on evidence that it was an erroneous reading.",
      "date": "2012"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Current Record Under Scrutiny",
      "text": "The legitimacy of the 1913 record measured in Death Valley has been questioned by several meteorological experts due to similar irregularities. However, the WMO has maintained it as the official record pending any future investigations.",
      "date": "2012"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Potential Tie for Highest Temperature",
      "text": "If the current record were to be decertified, the highest temperature would be a tie at 54.0 °C (129.2 °F), recorded both at Furnace Creek and in Kuwait.",
      "date": "2012"
    }
  ]
}

