      "headline": "Proposition of Lemuria",
      "text": "In 1864, zoologist Philip Sclater proposed the existence of a lost continent named Lemuria. He theorized that it had sunk beneath the Indian Ocean to explain the distribution of lemurs and other species.",
      "date": "1864"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption by Occultists",
      "text": "In the late 19th and early 20th centuries, the concept of Lemuria was adopted by occultists and theosophists, who incorporated it into their mythologies as a supposed ancient civilization and a part of human origins.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discreditation by Plate Tectonics",
      "text": "In the 20th century, the theory of Lemuria was discredited with the discovery of plate tectonics and continental drift, which provided a scientific explanation for the distribution of species without the need for a sunken continent.",
      "date": "1960"
