      "text": "The Kuiper belt formed as a circumstellar disc in the outer Solar System, extending from the orbit of Neptune at 30 astronomical units (AU) to approximately 50 AU from the Sun. This occurred during the early formation of the Solar System, around 4.6 billion years ago.",
