      "text": "On August 30, 1992, astronomers David Jewitt and Jane Luu discovered 1992 QB1, the first trans-Neptunian object to be found after Pluto and Charon, confirming the existence of the Kuiper belt.",
      "date": "1992-08-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Recognition of the Kuiper Belt",
      "text": "By the mid-1990s, the Kuiper belt was widely recognized as a distinct region of the Solar System, home to many small icy bodies.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
