    {
      "headline": "Renaming of the Play",
      "text": "Originally titled simply Oedipus, the play was later renamed Oedipus Tyrannus to distinguish it from Sophocles' later play, Oedipus at Colonus. The term 'tyrant' in antiquity referred to a ruler without a legitimate claim to rule, without necessarily having a negative connotation.",
      "date": "-0429"
    }
