      "headline": "Public Ministry Begins",
      "text": "Jesus began his public ministry, preaching about the Kingdom of God, performing miracles, and gathering disciples. This period lasted approximately three years.",
      "date": "0027"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sermon on the Mount",
      "text": "Jesus delivered the Sermon on the Mount, which includes many of his teachings and parables, such as the Beatitudes. This event is believed to have occurred early in his ministry.",
      "date": "0028"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Transfiguration",
      "text": "The Transfiguration of Jesus is an event where Jesus is transfigured and becomes radiant on a mountain. This event is described in the Synoptic Gospels.",
      "date": "0029"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Triumphal Entry into Jerusalem",
      "text": "Jesus entered Jerusalem riding a donkey, an event celebrated as Palm Sunday. This occurred shortly before his crucifixion.",
      "date": "0030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Last Supper",
      "text": "Jesus shared the Last Supper with his disciples, instituting the Eucharist. This event took place on the evening before his crucifixion.",
      "date": "0030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Crucifixion",
      "text": "Jesus was crucified under the order of Pontius Pilate. This event is central to Christian belief, occurring on Good Friday.",
      "date": "0030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Resurrection",
      "text": "According to Christian belief, Jesus rose from the dead on the third day after his crucifixion, an event celebrated as Easter Sunday.",
      "date": "0030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ascension",
      "text": "Jesus ascended into heaven 40 days after his resurrection, marking the end of his earthly ministry.",
      "date": "0030"
    }
  ]
}

