    {
      "headline": "Journey to the Holy Land",
      "text": "In 1523, Ignatius traveled to the Holy Land with the intention of settling there, but was advised by the Franciscans to return to Europe.",
      "date": "1523"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Studies in Paris",
      "text": "Ignatius began his studies at the University of Paris in 1528, where he met his future companions who would join him in founding the Society of Jesus.",
      "date": "1528"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of the Society of Jesus",
      "text": "On August 15, 1534, Ignatius and six companions, including Francis Xavier, took vows of poverty and chastity and committed to forming the Society of Jesus.",
