      "headline": "Formation of the Moon",
      "text": "Following the collision with Earth, the ejected debris from Theia and Earth coalesced to form the Moon. This event is a significant part of the giant-impact hypothesis.",
      "date": "-4500000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Remnants in Earth's Mantle",
      "text": "Collision simulations support the idea that the large low-shear-velocity provinces in the lower mantle of Earth may be remnants of Theia.",
      "date": "-4500000000"
    }
  ]
}

