            "headline": "First Practical Optical Fiber",
            "text": "In 1956, Basil Hirschowitz, C. Wilbur Peters, and Lawrence E. Curtiss created the first practical optical fiber, which was used for medical imaging.",
            "date": "1956"
        },
        {
            "headline": "Development of Low-Loss Optical Fiber",
            "text": "In 1970, researchers Robert D. Maurer, Donald Keck, Peter C. Schultz, and Frank Zimar at Corning Glass Works developed the first low-loss optical fiber, which could transmit light with less than 20 dB/km of attenuation.",
            "date": "1970"
        },
        {
            "headline": "First Optical Fiber Communication System",
            "text": "In 1977, the first live telephone traffic through fiber optics was conducted in Long Beach, California.",
            "date": "1977"
        },
        {
            "headline": "Introduction of Single-Mode Fiber",
            "text": "In 1983, single-mode optical fiber was introduced, which allowed for higher bandwidth and longer transmission distances compared to multi-mode fibers.",
            "date": "1983"
        },
        {
            "headline": "Development of Dense Wavelength Division Multiplexing (DWDM)",
            "text": "In the 1990s, Dense Wavelength Division Multiplexing (DWDM) technology was developed, significantly increasing the capacity of optical fiber networks by allowing multiple signals to be transmitted simultaneously on different wavelengths.",
            "date": "1990"
        },
        {
            "headline": "Deployment of Transatlantic Fiber Optic Cables",
            "text": "In the late 1990s, transatlantic fiber optic cables were deployed, greatly enhancing global communication capabilities.",
            "date": "1990"
        },
        {
            "headline": "Advancements in Fiber Optic Sensors",
            "text": "In the 2000s, advancements in fiber optic sensors were made, leading to their use in various applications such as structural health monitoring and environmental sensing.",
            "date": "2000"
        },
        {
            "headline": "Development of Photonic Crystal Fibers",
            "text": "In the early 2000s, photonic crystal fibers were developed, offering new possibilities in fiber optics due to their unique light-guiding properties.",
            "date": "2000"
        }
