      "text": "On August 21, 1992, deputies of the United States Marshals Service (USMS) attempted to arrest Randy Weaver at his cabin in Boundary County, Idaho, leading to the beginning of the Ruby Ridge standoff.",
      "date": "1992-08-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Samuel Weaver and Deputy Marshal",
      "text": "On August 21, 1992, during the initial encounter, a shootout occurred resulting in the deaths of Randy Weaver's 14-year-old son, Samuel Weaver, and Deputy U.S. Marshal William Degan.",
      "date": "1992-08-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "FBI Sniper Shoots Vicki Weaver",
      "text": "On August 22, 1992, an FBI sniper shot and killed Vicki Weaver, Randy Weaver's wife, while she was holding their infant daughter.",
      "date": "1992-08-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Ruby Ridge Standoff",
      "text": "The standoff ended on August 31, 1992, when Randy Weaver and his family surrendered to authorities.",
      "date": "1992-08-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Randy Weaver's Trial",
      "text": "In 1993, Randy Weaver was acquitted of all charges except for the original failure to appear in court and violating bail conditions. He was sentenced to 18 months in prison and fined $10,000.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Settlement with Weaver Family",
      "text": "In 1995, the U.S. government awarded the Weaver family $3.1 million in a settlement for the wrongful deaths of Vicki and Samuel Weaver.",
      "date": "1995"
    }
  ]
}

