      "headline": "Start of the Battle of Dunkirk",
      "text": "The Battle of Dunkirk began on 26 May 1940, as the Allies initiated Operation Dynamo to evacuate British and other Allied forces from the French port of Dunkirk.",
      "date": "1940-05-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Evacuation Efforts Intensify",
      "text": "On 27 May 1940, the evacuation efforts intensified as more ships were sent to rescue the trapped Allied forces. The operation faced challenges due to German air attacks and artillery fire.",
      "date": "1940-05-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Heavy Bombardment",
      "text": "On 29 May 1940, Dunkirk experienced heavy bombardment from German forces, causing significant damage to the town and port facilities, complicating the evacuation process.",
      "date": "1940-05-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Civilian Boats Join the Rescue",
      "text": "On 30 May 1940, civilian boats, famously known as the 'Little Ships of Dunkirk,' joined the rescue operation, significantly increasing the number of troops evacuated.",
      "date": "1940-05-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peak of Evacuation",
      "text": "On 31 May 1940, the evacuation reached its peak, with the largest number of troops being evacuated in a single day.",
      "date": "1940-05-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Battle of Dunkirk",
      "text": "The Battle of Dunkirk ended on 4 June 1940, with the successful evacuation of over 338,000 Allied soldiers, marking the conclusion of Operation Dynamo.",
      "date": "1940-06-04"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
