      "headline": "Acquisition of Tappan",
      "text": "In 1978, Icahn made a significant investment in Tappan, a manufacturer of stoves and ovens, and later sold it to Electrolux in 1979 for a substantial profit.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hostile Takeover of Trans World Airlines (TWA)",
      "text": "In 1985, Carl Icahn launched a hostile takeover of Trans World Airlines (TWA), which he successfully acquired, marking one of his most notable early corporate raids.",
      "date": "1985"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of Icahn Enterprises",
      "text": "Carl Icahn founded Icahn Enterprises in 1987, a diversified conglomerate holding company.",
      "date": "1987"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Investment in RJR Nabisco",
      "text": "In 1988, Icahn invested in RJR Nabisco, a major food and tobacco company, during its leveraged buyout, which was one of the largest in history at the time.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Acquisition of American Railcar Industries",
      "text": "In 1994, Icahn acquired American Railcar Industries, a manufacturer of railroad freight cars.",
      "date": "1994"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Investment in Netflix",
      "text": "In 2012, Carl Icahn made a significant investment in Netflix, which later proved to be highly profitable as the company's stock value increased substantially.",
      "date": "2012"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Advisor to President Donald Trump",
      "text": "In December 2016, Carl Icahn was named a special advisor to President Donald Trump on regulatory reform.",
      "date": "2016-12"
    },
