      "text": "Construction of the Bastille began in 1370 under the orders of Charles V of France. It was initially intended to defend the eastern approach to the city of Paris from the English during the Hundred Years' War.",
      "date": "1370"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Bastille",
      "text": "The Bastille was completed in 1383. It was a formidable fortress with eight towers and thick walls, serving as a defense for Paris and later as a state prison.",
      "date": "1383"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bastille Used as a State Prison",
      "text": "By the 17th century, the Bastille had become a state prison used by the kings of France to detain political prisoners, religious dissenters, and other individuals considered a threat to the state.",
      "date": "1600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Storming of the Bastille",
      "text": "On 14 July 1789, the Bastille was stormed by a revolutionary crowd. This event marked the beginning of the French Revolution and became a symbol of the end of the king's absolute power.",
      "date": "1789-07-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Demolition of the Bastille",
      "text": "Following its capture, the Bastille was demolished between 1789 and 1790. The site was later transformed into the Place de la Bastille, a public square.",
      "date": "1790"
    }
  ]
}

