      "text": "On April 16, 1947, the Texas City disaster took place when a fire aboard the French-registered vessel SS Grandcamp detonated approximately 2,300 tons of ammonium nitrate. The explosion killed at least 581 people and injured over 5,000, causing widespread destruction in Texas City, Texas.",
      "date": "1947-04-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Port Chicago Disaster",
      "text": "On July 17, 1944, the Port Chicago disaster occurred at the Port Chicago Naval Magazine in California. An explosion of munitions being loaded onto a cargo vessel killed 320 sailors and civilians and injured 390 others. It was the deadliest home front disaster of World War II in the United States.",
      "date": "1944-07-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Oppau Explosion",
      "text": "On September 21, 1921, the Oppau explosion happened at a BASF plant in Oppau, Germany. A tower silo storing a mixture of ammonium sulfate and ammonium nitrate exploded, killing 500-600 people and injuring about 2,000. The explosion was felt over a large area and caused significant damage.",
      "date": "1921-09-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cleveland East Ohio Gas Explosion",
      "text": "On October 20, 1944, the Cleveland East Ohio Gas Explosion occurred when a liquefied natural gas tank exploded in Cleveland, Ohio. The explosion and resulting fires killed 130 people and destroyed a large part of the surrounding neighborhood.",
      "date": "1944-10-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "PEPCON Disaster",
      "text": "On May 4, 1988, the PEPCON disaster took place in Henderson, Nevada, when a fire caused the detonation of approximately 4,500 tons of ammonium perchlorate. The explosion killed two people, injured 372, and caused extensive damage to the surrounding area.",
      "date": "1988-05-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Enschede Fireworks Disaster",
      "text": "On May 13, 2000, the Enschede fireworks disaster occurred in Enschede, Netherlands. A fire at a fireworks depot led to an explosion that killed 23 people, injured nearly 1,000, and destroyed a large part of the city.",
      "date": "2000-05-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Tianjin Explosions",
      "text": "On August 12, 2015, a series of explosions occurred at a container storage station at the Port of Tianjin, China. The explosions killed 173 people, injured hundreds, and caused extensive damage to the port and surrounding areas.",
