      "text": "In 1152, Henry II married Eleanor of Aquitaine, acquiring the Duchy of Aquitaine and significantly expanding his territories.",
      "date": "1152"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Henry II Becomes King of England",
      "text": "Henry II succeeded his rival Stephen and became King of England in 1154, further consolidating his power and establishing the Angevin Empire.",
      "date": "1154"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Henry II's Reforms",
      "text": "During his reign, Henry II implemented significant legal and administrative reforms, including the development of the common law and the jury system.",
      "date": "1154"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conquest of Ireland",
      "text": "In 1171, Henry II invaded Ireland, establishing English control over parts of the island and expanding the Angevin Empire's influence.",
      "date": "1171"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rebellion of Henry's Sons",
      "text": "In 1173-1174, Henry II faced a rebellion led by his sons, supported by their mother Eleanor of Aquitaine, which was eventually suppressed.",
      "date": "1173"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Henry II",
      "text": "Henry II died on July 6, 1189, marking the end of his reign and the beginning of his son Richard I's rule.",
      "date": "1189-07-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Richard I's Crusade",
      "text": "Richard I, also known as Richard the Lionheart, participated in the Third Crusade from 1189 to 1192, leaving the Angevin Empire under the administration of his brother John.",
      "date": "1189"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Normandy",
      "text": "In 1204, King John lost the Duchy of Normandy to the French King Philip II, significantly reducing the Angevin Empire's territories.",
