      "headline": "Development of Fortran Begins",
      "text": "In 1953, John Backus proposed to his superiors at IBM to develop a more practical alternative to assembly language for programming the IBM 704 mainframe computer. This proposal led to the development of Fortran.",
      "date": "1953"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran I Released",
      "text": "In 1957, the first version of Fortran, known as Fortran I, was released. It was the first high-level programming language and was designed for scientific and engineering calculations.",
      "date": "1957"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran II Released",
      "text": "In 1958, Fortran II was released. It included improvements such as the ability to compile separate subroutines independently.",
      "date": "1958"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran III Developed",
      "text": "In 1958, Fortran III was developed but never released as a product. It was an experimental version that included features for handling input/output operations.",
      "date": "1958"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran IV Standardized",
      "text": "In 1962, Fortran IV was developed and later standardized by the American National Standards Institute (ANSI) in 1966, making it the first standardized version of Fortran.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran 66 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 1966, the first official standard for Fortran, known as Fortran 66, was released by ANSI.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran 77 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 1978, Fortran 77 was released as a new standard, introducing features such as structured programming constructs and character string handling.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran 90 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 1991, Fortran 90 was released, introducing modern programming concepts such as array programming, modules, and recursion.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran 95 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 1997, Fortran 95 was released, which included minor improvements and clarifications to Fortran 90.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran 2003 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 2004, Fortran 2003 was released, adding support for object-oriented programming and interoperability with C.",
      "date": "2004"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran 2008 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 2010, Fortran 2008 was released, introducing features such as coarrays for parallel programming.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fortran 2018 Standard Released",
      "text": "In 2018, Fortran 2018 was released, which included further enhancements to parallel programming and other language features.",
      "date": "2018"
    }
  ]
}

