    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Harry Benjamin International Gender Dysphoria Association",
      "text": "In 1979, the Harry Benjamin International Gender Dysphoria Association was established, which later became known as the World Professional Association for Transgender Health (WPATH). This organization set standards of care for gender-affirming surgeries.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Standards of Care",
      "text": "In 1979, the first Standards of Care for the Health of Transsexual, Transgender, and Gender Nonconforming People were introduced by the Harry Benjamin International Gender Dysphoria Association, providing guidelines for gender-affirming surgeries.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Phalloplasty for Transgender Men",
      "text": "In the 1980s, the first phalloplasty procedures were developed specifically for transgender men, offering new surgical options for gender affirmation.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "WPATH Standards of Care Version 7",
      "text": "In 2011, the World Professional Association for Transgender Health (WPATH) released the seventh version of its Standards of Care, which included updated guidelines for gender-affirming surgeries.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Medicare Coverage for Gender-Affirming Surgery",
      "text": "In 2014, the United States Medicare program lifted its ban on covering gender-affirming surgeries, allowing more transgender individuals access to these procedures.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
