      "headline": "Proclamation of the Second Spanish Republic",
      "text": "The Second Spanish Republic was proclaimed on 14 April 1931 following the deposition of King Alfonso XIII.",
      "date": "1931-04-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Constitution of 1931",
      "text": "In December 1931, the new constitution of the Second Spanish Republic was approved, establishing a secular and democratic state.",
      "date": "1931-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reforms and Political Changes",
      "text": "Throughout the early 1930s, the Republic implemented various reforms, including agrarian reform, military reform, and educational reform, aiming to modernize Spain.",
      "date": "1931"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Asturias Miners' Strike",
      "text": "In October 1934, a major strike by miners in Asturias was violently suppressed by the government, highlighting social tensions within the Republic.",
      "date": "1934-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Popular Front Victory",
      "text": "In February 1936, the leftist Popular Front coalition won the general elections, leading to increased political polarization.",
      "date": "1936-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Outbreak of the Spanish Civil War",
      "text": "The Spanish Civil War began on 17 July 1936, following a military uprising against the Republic led by General Francisco Franco.",
      "date": "1936-07-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Second Spanish Republic",
      "text": "The Second Spanish Republic was dissolved on 1 April 1939 after surrendering to the Nationalists led by General Francisco Franco, marking the end of the Spanish Civil War.",
      "date": "1939-04-01"
    }
  ]
}

{
