    },
    {
      "headline": "Sinking of the RMS Lusitania",
      "text": "On 1915-05-07, the RMS Lusitania was torpedoed by the German U-boat U-20 off the coast of Ireland. The ship sank in 18 minutes, resulting in the deaths of 1,198 passengers and crew.",
      "date": "1915-05-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Aftermath and International Reaction",
      "text": "The sinking of the Lusitania on 1915-05-07 caused international outrage, particularly in the United States, and contributed to shifting public opinion against Germany during World War I.",
      "date": "1915-05-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Impact on U.S. Involvement in World War I",
      "text": "The sinking of the Lusitania on 1915-05-07 was a significant factor in the United States' decision to enter World War I in 1917, as it highlighted the dangers of unrestricted submarine warfare.",
