      "headline": "Civil Rights Act of 1964",
      "text": "On July 2, 1964, the Civil Rights Act was signed into law, prohibiting discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, or national origin, and ending unequal application of voter registration requirements and racial segregation in schools, at the workplace, and by facilities that served the general public.",
      "date": "1964-07-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voting Rights Act of 1965",
      "text": "On August 6, 1965, the Voting Rights Act was signed into law, aiming to overcome legal barriers at the state and local levels that prevented African Americans from exercising their right to vote under the 15th Amendment.",
      "date": "1965-08-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fair Housing Act",
      "text": "On April 11, 1968, the Fair Housing Act was enacted as part of the Civil Rights Act of 1968, providing for equal housing opportunities regardless of race, religion, or national origin and making it a crime to interfere with housing rights.",
      "date": "1968-04-11"
    }
  ]
}

