      "text": "In 1542, the Spanish crown issued the New Laws of the Indies, aimed at protecting indigenous peoples from exploitation and abuse by Spanish settlers.",
      "date": "1542"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Viceroyalty of New Spain",
      "text": "In 1535, the Spanish crown established the Viceroyalty of New Spain, encompassing territories in North America, Central America, and the Caribbean.",
      "date": "1535"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Viceroyalty of Peru",
      "text": "In 1542, the Viceroyalty of Peru was established, consolidating Spanish control over South American territories.",
      "date": "1542"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Spanish Colonial Rule",
      "text": "In 1898, the Spanish-American War resulted in Spain losing its last territories in the Americas, marking the end of Spanish colonial rule in the region.",
      "date": "1898"
    }
  ]
}

