      "headline": "Breton Language Origins",
      "text": "Breton originated from the migration of Britons from Great Britain to Armorica (modern-day Brittany) during the early Middle Ages. It is a Southwestern Brittonic language of the Celtic language group.",
      "date": "-0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Early Medieval Period",
      "text": "Breton began to be used in Brittany as the Britons settled in the region, gradually replacing the Gaulish language.",
