      "text": "Breton literature began to flourish during the medieval period, with notable works such as the 'Lais of Marie de France' which were composed in the 12th century.",
      "date": "1100"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Breton Language in the Middle Ages",
      "text": "During the Middle Ages, Breton was widely spoken in Brittany and was used in various forms of literature and legal documents.",
      "date": "1200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline in Use",
      "text": "The use of Breton began to decline in the 16th century as French became more dominant in administrative and official contexts.",
      "date": "1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "19th Century Revival Efforts",
      "text": "In the 19th century, there were efforts to revive the Breton language, including the collection and publication of Breton folklore and literature.",
