      "headline": "Introduction of Formula One",
      "text": "Formula One, as a racing category, was introduced in 1947, establishing a set of regulations for engine capacity and other technical specifications.",
      "date": "1947"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Formula One World Championship",
      "text": "The first Formula One World Championship was held in 1950, marking the beginning of the official championship series.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of 1.5-litre Formula",
      "text": "In 1961, Formula One introduced a new engine regulation, limiting engine capacity to 1.5 litres, which lasted until 1965.",
      "date": "1961"
    },
