      "headline": "Establishment of the European Commission",
      "text": "The European Commission was established in 1958 as the executive branch of the European Economic Community (EEC), which later became the European Union (EU).",
      "date": "1958"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Merger Treaty",
      "text": "In 1967, the Merger Treaty came into effect, combining the executive bodies of the European Coal and Steel Community (ECSC), the European Atomic Energy Community (Euratom), and the European Economic Community (EEC) into a single Commission.",
      "date": "1967"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Single European Act",
      "text": "The Single European Act, which came into force in 1987, significantly increased the powers of the European Commission, particularly in the area of internal market regulation.",
      "date": "1987"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Maastricht Treaty",
      "text": "The Maastricht Treaty, signed in 1992 and effective from 1993, transformed the European Economic Community into the European Union and expanded the Commission's powers in new areas such as foreign policy and justice.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Amsterdam Treaty",
      "text": "The Amsterdam Treaty, which came into force in 1999, further reformed the European Commission by enhancing its role in areas such as employment and social policy.",
      "date": "1999"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nice Treaty",
      "text": "The Nice Treaty, effective from 2003, reformed the institutional structure of the EU, including changes to the composition and functioning of the European Commission.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lisbon Treaty",
      "text": "The Lisbon Treaty, which came into force in 2009, introduced significant changes to the European Commission, including the creation of the position of High Representative of the Union for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Current Composition",
      "text": "As of 2023, the European Commission is composed of 27 Commissioners, including the President, representing each EU member state.",
      "date": "2023"
    }
  ]
}

