      "headline": "Wolf's Sunspot Number",
      "text": "In 1848, Rudolf Wolf introduced the Wolf sunspot number, a way to quantify sunspot activity, which became a standard measure for solar cycles.",
      "date": "1848"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Solar Cycle 1",
      "text": "The first solar cycle, known as Solar Cycle 1, began in 1755 and ended in 1766. It was the first cycle to be recorded using systematic observations.",
      "date": "1755"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Solar Cycle 24",
      "text": "Solar Cycle 24 began in December 2008 and ended in December 2019. It was characterized by a relatively low number of sunspots compared to previous cycles.",
      "date": "2008-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Solar Cycle 25",
      "text": "Solar Cycle 25 began in December 2019. It is expected to reach its maximum around 2025.",
      "date": "2019-12"
    }
  ]
}

