      "text": "Siddhartha Gautama, who would later become known as the Buddha, was born in Lumbini, in what is now Nepal, to royal parents of the Shakya clan. The exact date of his birth is uncertain, but it is traditionally dated to the 6th or 5th century BCE.",
      "date": "-0563"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renunciation of Home Life",
      "text": "At the age of 29, Siddhartha Gautama renounced his royal life to become a wandering ascetic, seeking to understand the nature of suffering and the path to liberation.",
