      "text": "Eugène Delacroix painted 'Liberty Leading the People' in the autumn of 1830. The painting commemorates the July Revolution of 1830 in France, which resulted in the overthrow of King Charles X.",
      "date": "1830"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exhibition at the Salon",
      "text": "The painting was first exhibited at the Salon in 1831, where it received mixed reviews. Some praised its boldness and energy, while others criticized it for its perceived political radicalism.",
