      "headline": "First Reported Sighting",
      "text": "Gustave, the Nile crocodile, was first reported in the Ruzizi River and Lake Tanganyika region in Burundi. His large size and distinctive features made him easily recognizable.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Research and Documentation",
      "text": "In the late 1990s, Patrice Faye, a herpetologist, began studying Gustave. Faye documented Gustave's behavior and attempted to capture him for research purposes.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Failed Capture Attempt",
      "text": "In 2002, a team led by Patrice Faye attempted to capture Gustave using a large cage. Despite their efforts, Gustave evaded capture, further enhancing his mythical status.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Documentary Feature",
      "text": "In 2004, Gustave was featured in a documentary titled 'Capturing the Killer Croc,' which aired on PBS. The documentary highlighted the challenges of capturing such a large and elusive crocodile.",
      "date": "2004"
    },
