      "headline": "Completion of Borobudur",
      "text": "Borobudur was completed in the year 825. It is a Mahayana Buddhist temple and is renowned for its intricate carvings and massive structure.",
      "date": "0825"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abandonment of Borobudur",
      "text": "Borobudur was abandoned in the 14th century as the Javanese converted to Islam. The temple was left to be covered by volcanic ash and jungle growth.",
      "date": "1400"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rediscovery of Borobudur",
      "text": "In 1814, Borobudur was rediscovered by Sir Thomas Stamford Raffles, the British ruler of Java, who was informed of its existence by native Indonesians.",
      "date": "1814"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration of Borobudur",
      "text": "The first major restoration of Borobudur was carried out between 1907 and 1911 under the supervision of Theodoor van Erp, a Dutch engineer.",
      "date": "1907"
    },
    {
      "headline": "UNESCO World Heritage Site Designation",
      "text": "In 1991, Borobudur was designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, recognizing its cultural significance and historical importance.",
      "date": "1991"
    }
  ]
