      "headline": "Incorporation into the Macedonian Empire",
      "text": "In 342 BCE, Thrace was conquered by Philip II of Macedon, father of Alexander the Great, and became part of the Macedonian Empire.",
      "date": "-0342"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Conquest",
      "text": "In 46 CE, Thrace was annexed by the Roman Empire and became the Roman province of Thracia.",
      "date": "0046"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Division of the Roman Empire",
      "text": "In 395 CE, the Roman Empire was divided, and Thrace became part of the Eastern Roman Empire, also known as the Byzantine Empire.",
