      "headline": "Establishment of Westchester County",
      "text": "Westchester County was established in 1683 as one of the original counties of the Province of New York. It was named after the city of Chester in England.",
      "date": "1683"
    },
    {
      "headline": "American Revolutionary War Impact",
      "text": "During the American Revolutionary War, Westchester County was a significant battleground due to its strategic location between British-held New York City and the American-controlled Hudson Valley. Notable events include the Battle of White Plains in 1776.",
      "date": "1776"
    },
    {
      "headline": "County Seat Designation",
      "text": "White Plains was designated as the county seat of Westchester County. This designation has played a crucial role in the administrative and judicial functions of the county.",
      "date": "1778"
    },
