      "text": "In 1912, the United States intervened in Nicaragua to support the government against a rebellion, establishing a long-term military presence and influence in the country's politics.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mexican Revolution Intervention",
      "text": "During the Mexican Revolution, the United States intervened in 1914 by occupying the port city of Veracruz, aiming to influence the outcome of the revolution and protect American interests.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Occupation of Haiti",
      "text": "The United States occupied Haiti from 1915 to 1934, following political instability and violence. The occupation aimed to stabilize the country and protect American interests.",
      "date": "1915"
