      "text": "In 1982, the FARC held its Seventh Guerrilla Conference, where it decided to expand its operations and increase its military capabilities.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Patriotic Union",
      "text": "In 1985, the FARC participated in the creation of the Patriotic Union (Unión Patriótica), a political party intended to participate in Colombian politics.",
      "date": "1985"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peace Talks with Colombian Government",
      "text": "In 1999, peace talks began between the FARC and the Colombian government, aiming to end the ongoing conflict.",
      "date": "1999"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Jaque",
      "text": "On July 2, 2008, the Colombian military conducted Operation Jaque, successfully rescuing 15 hostages held by the FARC, including former presidential candidate Ingrid Betancourt.",
      "date": "2008-07-02"
