      "headline": "Publication of RFC 791",
      "text": "In September 1981, the Internet Protocol version 4 (IPv4) was formally defined in RFC 791. This document outlined the technical specifications of IPv4, which became the foundation for the Internet.",
      "date": "1981-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of IPv6",
      "text": "The Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) was introduced in December 1998 as a successor to IPv4. IPv6 was designed to address the issue of IPv4 address exhaustion by providing a vastly larger address space.",
      "date": "1998-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IPv6 Launch Day",
      "text": "On June 6, 2012, the World IPv6 Launch Day was held, marking the official launch of IPv6 by major Internet service providers, networking equipment manufacturers, and web companies.",
