      "headline": "Founding of BASF",
      "text": "BASF was founded on April 6, 1865, by Friedrich Engelhorn in Mannheim, Germany. The company was initially established to produce dyes.",
      "date": "1865-04-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Relocation to Ludwigshafen",
      "text": "In 1866, BASF moved its operations to Ludwigshafen, Germany, where it established its headquarters and main production facilities.",
      "date": "1866"
