      "headline": "Development of the Haber-Bosch Process",
      "text": "In 1913, BASF began industrial production of ammonia using the Haber-Bosch process, which was crucial for fertilizer production and had a significant impact on agriculture.",
      "date": "1913"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of IG Farben",
      "text": "In 1925, BASF merged with several other chemical companies to form IG Farben, which became the largest chemical company in the world at the time.",
      "date": "1925"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-establishment as BASF",
      "text": "After World War II, IG Farben was dissolved, and BASF was re-established as an independent company in 1952.",
      "date": "1952"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion into North America",
      "text": "In the 1960s, BASF expanded its operations into North America, establishing a significant presence in the United States.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Acquisition of Engelhard Corporation",
      "text": "In 2006, BASF acquired Engelhard Corporation, a leading supplier of catalysts and specialty chemicals, enhancing its portfolio in the chemical industry.",
      "date": "2006"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Acquisition of Ciba",
      "text": "In 2009, BASF acquired Ciba, a Swiss specialty chemicals company, further expanding its product offerings and market reach.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Divestiture of Construction Chemicals",
      "text": "In 2020, BASF completed the sale of its Construction Chemicals business to an affiliate of Lone Star, a global private equity firm.",
      "date": "2020"
