      "headline": "Bill Gates Endorses Khan Academy",
      "text": "In 2010, Bill Gates publicly endorsed Khan Academy, stating that he used the videos to teach his own children. This endorsement significantly increased the organization's visibility.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Google Donates to Khan Academy",
      "text": "In 2010, Google announced a $2 million donation to Khan Academy as part of its Project 10^100, to support the creation of new courses and translation into other languages.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Khan Academy Launches Official Website",
      "text": "In 2011, Khan Academy launched its official website, offering a wide range of educational resources including video lessons and practice exercises.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Khan Academy Partners with the College Board",
      "text": "In 2015, Khan Academy partnered with the College Board to provide free, official SAT practice resources, making test preparation more accessible to students.",
      "date": "2015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Khan Academy Expands to Include More Subjects",
      "text": "By 2017, Khan Academy had expanded its offerings to include over 10,000 video lessons covering a wide array of subjects such as mathematics, sciences, literature, history, and computer science.",
      "date": "2017"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Khan Academy Launches Khan Academy Kids",
      "text": "In 2018, Khan Academy launched Khan Academy Kids, a free educational program designed to inspire young children to become learners for life.",
      "date": "2018"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Khan Academy's Role During COVID-19 Pandemic",
      "text": "In 2020, during the COVID-19 pandemic, Khan Academy played a crucial role in providing free educational resources to students worldwide as schools shifted to remote learning.",
      "date": "2020"
    }
  ]
}

