      "headline": "Origin of the Term 'Jaywalking'",
      "text": "The term 'jaywalking' originated in the United States as a derivation of the phrase 'jay-drivers', which referred to people who drove horse-drawn carriages and automobiles on the wrong side of the road. It later took on its current meaning related to pedestrians.",
      "date": "1910"
