      "headline": "Rise of Automobiles and Pedestrian Conflicts",
      "text": "With the rise of automobiles in the early 20th century, conflicts between pedestrians and vehicles increased. This led to the need for regulations and the popularization of the term 'jaywalking' to describe pedestrians crossing roads in violation of traffic rules.",
      "date": "1920"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Campaigns Against Jaywalking",
      "text": "In the 1920s and 1930s, automobile associations and manufacturers launched campaigns to promote road safety and discourage jaywalking, framing it as a dangerous and socially unacceptable behavior.",
      "date": "1920-1930"
    },
