      "headline": "Establishment of Las Palmas",
      "text": "Las Palmas de Gran Canaria was founded on June 24, 1478, by Juan Rejón, head of the invading Castilian army.",
      "date": "1478-06-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Las Palmas",
      "text": "In 1595, the Battle of Las Palmas took place when English privateers led by Francis Drake attempted to invade the island but were repelled by the local population.",
      "date": "1595"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Attack by Dutch Forces",
      "text": "In 1599, a Dutch fleet led by Pieter van der Does attacked Las Palmas but was eventually defeated.",
      "date": "1599"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Economic Growth in the 19th Century",
      "text": "During the 19th century, Gran Canaria experienced significant economic growth due to the export of cochineal dye and the development of the port of Las Palmas.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Tourism Boom",
      "text": "In the 1960s, Gran Canaria began to develop as a major tourist destination, leading to rapid economic and infrastructural development.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
