      "headline": "Foundation of Dehradun",
      "text": "Dehradun was founded in the 18th century by Guru Ram Rai, the eldest son of the seventh Sikh Guru, Guru Har Rai. He established a 'Dera' (camp) in the 'Doon' valley, which led to the name Dehradun.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Annexation",
      "text": "In 1816, after the Anglo-Nepalese War, the British East India Company annexed Dehradun as part of the Treaty of Sugauli.",
      "date": "1816"
