      "headline": "Synod of Dort",
      "text": "The Synod of Dort was held from 1618 to 1619 in the Netherlands. It was a significant event for Reformed Christianity, where the doctrines of Calvinism were affirmed and the Five Points of Calvinism were articulated.",
      "date": "1618"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Westminster Assembly",
      "text": "The Westminster Assembly took place from 1643 to 1653 in England, producing the Westminster Confession of Faith, which became a key doctrinal standard for many Reformed churches.",
      "date": "1643"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Heidelberg Catechism",
      "text": "The Heidelberg Catechism was adopted in 1563 as a teaching tool for Reformed churches, particularly in the Palatinate region of Germany.",
      "date": "1563"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the World Communion of Reformed Churches",
      "text": "In 2010, the World Communion of Reformed Churches was formed, uniting over 80 million Reformed Christians worldwide.",
      "date": "2010"
    }
  ]
}

