      "text": "On June 20, 2018, President Trump signed an executive order to end the family separation policy, responding to the intense public and political pressure.",
      "date": "2018-06-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Court Order to Reunite Families",
      "text": "On June 26, 2018, a federal judge ordered the Trump administration to reunite separated families within 30 days, with children under five to be reunited within 14 days.",
      "date": "2018-06-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Missed Reunification Deadlines",
      "text": "By July 2018, the administration missed the court-imposed deadlines to reunite all separated families, citing difficulties in locating some parents who had already been deported.",
      "date": "2018-07"
