      "headline": "Earliest Recorded Exorcisms",
      "text": "Exorcisms have been practiced since ancient times, with some of the earliest recorded exorcisms found in the Sumerian culture, where priests would perform rituals to expel demons.",
      "date": "-3000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exorcism in Ancient Egypt",
      "text": "In ancient Egypt, exorcisms were performed by priests who used spells and incantations to drive out evil spirits from individuals.",
      "date": "-1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exorcism in the Hebrew Bible",
      "text": "The Hebrew Bible contains references to exorcisms, such as the story of David playing the harp to soothe King Saul, who was troubled by an evil spirit.",
      "date": "-1000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exorcism in the New Testament",
      "text": "The New Testament of the Christian Bible contains several accounts of Jesus performing exorcisms, casting out demons from possessed individuals.",
      "date": "0030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exorcism in Early Christianity",
      "text": "In the early Christian church, exorcism became a formalized ritual, with specific prayers and rites developed to expel demons.",
      "date": "0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exorcism in the Middle Ages",
      "text": "During the Middle Ages, exorcism was a common practice in the Catholic Church, often performed by priests using holy water, prayers, and the sign of the cross.",
      "date": "1000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rituale Romanum Published",
      "text": "In 1614, the Catholic Church published the Rituale Romanum, which included the official rite of exorcism, providing a standardized procedure for priests to follow.",
      "date": "1614"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exorcism in the Modern Era",
      "text": "In the modern era, exorcism continues to be practiced in various religious traditions, although it is often viewed with skepticism by the scientific community.",
      "date": "1900"
