      "headline": "First Appearance of Theropods",
      "text": "Theropods first appeared during the Carnian age of the late Triassic period, approximately 231.4 million years ago.",
      "date": "-231400000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dominance of Theropods",
      "text": "Theropods included the majority of large terrestrial carnivores from the Early Jurassic period, which began around 201.3 million years ago, until at least the close of the Cretaceous period.",
      "date": "-201300000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Evolution of Birds",
      "text": "In the Jurassic period, birds evolved from small specialized coelurosaurian theropods. This evolutionary transition marks a significant diversification within the theropod clade.",
      "date": "-145000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Cretaceous Period",
      "text": "The Cretaceous period ended about 66 million years ago, marking the extinction of many theropod species, although birds, as descendants of theropods, survived.",
      "date": "-66000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Representation of Theropods",
      "text": "Today, theropods are represented by about 11,000 living species of birds, showcasing the evolutionary success and adaptation of this clade.",
      "date": "2023"
    }
  ]
}

