      "headline": "Discovery of XYY Syndrome",
      "text": "XYY syndrome was first discovered in 1961 by Dr. Avery A. Sandberg and his colleagues at Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center in Buffalo, New York. They identified the extra Y chromosome in a male patient.",
      "date": "1961"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Initial Research and Misconceptions",
      "text": "In the 1960s and 1970s, initial research suggested that males with XYY syndrome might be more prone to aggressive behavior and criminal activity. These studies were later criticized for methodological flaws.",
      "date": "1960s-1970s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reevaluation of Behavioral Implications",
