      "headline": "2020 United States Presidential Election",
      "text": "The United States held its presidential election on November 3, 2020. Joe Biden defeated the incumbent president, Donald Trump, becoming the 46th president of the United States.",
      "date": "2020-11-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capitol Riot",
      "text": "On January 6, 2021, supporters of outgoing President Donald Trump stormed the United States Capitol in an attempt to overturn the 2020 presidential election results, leading to widespread condemnation and the second impeachment of Trump.",
      "date": "2021-01-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "COVID-19 Vaccination Campaigns",
      "text": "Mass vaccination campaigns against COVID-19 began globally in December 2020, with vaccines such as Pfizer-BioNTech, Moderna, and AstraZeneca being administered to combat the pandemic.",
      "date": "2020-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ever Given Suez Canal Obstruction",
      "text": "The Ever Given, a large container ship, became lodged in the Suez Canal on March 23, 2021, blocking one of the world's busiest trade routes for six days and causing a significant disruption in global shipping.",
      "date": "2021-03-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Taliban Takeover of Afghanistan",
      "text": "The Taliban regained control of Afghanistan on August 15, 2021, following the withdrawal of U.S. and NATO troops, leading to the collapse of the Afghan government.",
      "date": "2021-08-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "COP26 Climate Summit",
      "text": "The 26th UN Climate Change Conference of the Parties (COP26) was held in Glasgow, Scotland, from October 31 to November 12, 2021, focusing on global climate action and commitments to reduce carbon emissions.",
      "date": "2021-10-31"
