      "headline": "Invention of Sundials",
      "text": "Sundials, the earliest known time-measuring devices, were used by ancient Egyptians and Babylonians around 1500 BCE.",
      "date": "-1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Water Clocks in Ancient Egypt and Babylon",
      "text": "Water clocks, or clepsydrae, were used in ancient Egypt and Babylon around 1400 BCE to measure time by the flow of water.",
      "date": "-1400"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Mechanical Clocks",
      "text": "The first mechanical clocks were developed in Europe in the early 14th century, around 1300, using gears and weights.",
      "date": "1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Invention of the Pendulum Clock",
      "text": "In 1656, Dutch scientist Christiaan Huygens invented the pendulum clock, which greatly improved timekeeping accuracy.",
