      "text": "In 1984, another fatality occurred when a man died after his kayak tipped over and he was electrocuted by the water.",
      "date": "1984"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fifth Fatality",
      "text": "In 1987, a 18-year-old drowned in the Tidal Wave Pool, marking the fifth fatality at Action Park.",
      "date": "1987"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Closure of Action Park",
      "text": "Action Park closed in 1996 due to financial difficulties faced by its parent company, Great American Recreation.",
      "date": "1996"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reopening as Mountain Creek Waterpark",
      "text": "In 1998, the park reopened under new ownership as Mountain Creek Waterpark, with many of the original rides removed or modified for safety.",
      "date": "1998"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Brief Return of Action Park Name",
      "text": "In 2014, the park briefly revived the Action Park name, capitalizing on its nostalgic and infamous reputation.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Mountain Creek Name",
      "text": "In 2016, the park reverted to the Mountain Creek Waterpark name, ending the brief revival of the Action Park brand.",
      "date": "2016"
    }
  ]
}

