      "text": "In 1993, Urban Müller released a compiler for Brainfuck, which was only 240 bytes in size. This release demonstrated the language's minimalistic nature and efficiency.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Popularity in Esoteric Programming Community",
      "text": "Throughout the 1990s and 2000s, Brainfuck gained popularity within the esoteric programming community. Its simplicity and challenge attracted programmers interested in unconventional and minimalist coding.",
      "date": "1990s-2000s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Influence on Other Esoteric Languages",
      "text": "Brainfuck has influenced the creation of other esoteric programming languages, inspiring developers to explore the limits of minimalism and creativity in programming language design.",
      "date": "1990s-Present"
    }
  ]
}

