      "text": "The Federalist No. 51 was published on February 6, 1788. Written by James Madison, it explains the system of checks and balances and the separation of powers in the Constitution.",
      "date": "1788-02-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Final Essay Published",
      "text": "The final essay, The Federalist No. 85, was published on August 13, 1788. It was written by Alexander Hamilton and concludes the series by arguing for the ratification of the Constitution.",
      "date": "1788-08-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Federalist Papers Compilation",
      "text": "The essays were compiled into a book titled 'The Federalist' in 1788. This compilation helped to influence the ratification debates in New York.",
      "date": "1788"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the United States Constitution",
      "text": "The United States Constitution was ratified on June 21, 1788, after New Hampshire became the ninth state to ratify it, largely influenced by the arguments presented in The Federalist Papers.",
      "date": "1788-06-21"
    }
  ]
}

