      "text": "McMurdo Station was established in 1955 as part of the United States' efforts to support scientific research in Antarctica. It was named after Archibald McMurdo of the Royal Navy, who first charted the area in 1841.",
      "date": "1955"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Geophysical Year",
      "text": "During the International Geophysical Year (IGY) of 1957-1958, McMurdo Station played a crucial role in supporting scientific research and exploration in Antarctica. The IGY was a collaborative international scientific effort that marked a significant increase in Antarctic research.",
      "date": "1957"
    },
