      "headline": "RFC 765 - FTP Specification Update",
      "text": "In June 1980, FTP was updated with RFC 765, which included improvements and clarifications to the protocol.",
      "date": "1980-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "RFC 959 - FTP Standardization",
      "text": "In October 1985, FTP was further refined and standardized with the publication of RFC 959, which remains the current specification for FTP.",
      "date": "1985-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of FTPS",
      "text": "FTP Secure (FTPS) was introduced as an extension to FTP, adding support for the Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) cryptographic protocols to secure the data transfer.",
      "date": "1990s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of SFTP",
      "text": "The SSH File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) was developed as a more secure alternative to FTP, using the Secure Shell (SSH) protocol to provide encryption and secure file transfer.",
      "date": "1990s"
    }
  ]
}

