      "text": "The eleventh edition, published in 1911, is often considered a landmark edition due to its scholarly content and comprehensive coverage.",
      "date": "1911"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First American Edition",
      "text": "The first American edition of the Encyclopædia Britannica was published in 1901.",
      "date": "1901"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fifteenth Edition Published",
      "text": "The fifteenth edition, also known as the New Encyclopædia Britannica, was first published in 1974. It introduced a new structure with three parts: the Micropædia, Macropædia, and Propædia.",
      "date": "1974"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Last Printed Edition",
      "text": "The 2010 version of the fifteenth edition, which spans 32 volumes and 32,640 pages, was the last printed edition of the Encyclopædia Britannica.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Transition to Online Only",
      "text": "Since 2016, the Encyclopædia Britannica has been published exclusively as an online encyclopaedia, marking the end of its print editions.",
      "date": "2016"
    }
  ]
}

